# Branching and Merging – Detailed Execution (Git Bash)

## Run Step-by-Step

```bash id="c1"
# STEP 1: Check current branch
git branch
```

```bash id="c2"
# STEP 2: Create new branch
git branch GitNewBranch
```

```bash id="c3"
# STEP 3: List all branches
git branch -a
```

```bash id="c4"
# STEP 4: Switch to new branch
git checkout GitNewBranch
```

```bash id="c5"
# STEP 5: Create new file in branch
touch branchfile.txt
```

```bash id="c6"
# STEP 6: Add content to file
echo "This is created in GitNewBranch" > branchfile.txt
```

```bash id="c7"
# STEP 7: Add file to staging
git add .
```

```bash id="c8"
# STEP 8: Commit changes
git commit -m "Added file in GitNewBranch"
```

```bash id="c9"
# STEP 9: Check status
git status
```

```bash id="c10"
# STEP 10: Switch back to main branch
git checkout main
```

```bash id="c11"
# STEP 11: See differences between main and branch
git diff main GitNewBranch
```

```bash id="c12"
# STEP 12: Merge branch into main
git merge GitNewBranch
```

```bash id="c13"
# STEP 13: View commit graph
git log --oneline --graph --decorate
```

```bash id="c14"
# STEP 14: Delete branch after merge
git branch -d GitNewBranch
```

```bash id="c15"
# STEP 15: Final status
git status
```

```bash id="c16"
# STEP 16: Push to GitHub
git push
```

---

## Final Result

* Branch created
* File added in branch
* Changes committed
* Branch merged into main
* Branch deleted
